reims-vgpu: render Stores whose readback does not block the drain.

Before: on the copying rail (every Store on the Linux phone host, whose
shared guest RAM RADV will not import) a render Store recorded the copy of
its resident into a staging buffer, waited the fence on the drain worker,
and then wrote the guest's pages. Under heavy load: drain busy
808 ms/s, ~460 ms of it in that wait (`readback_split fence_us`), the GPU
busy 17 ms/s - submission and wake latency, sat out holding the device lock
and the QEMU main loop.
Now: the surface Store arm (`M2vDrawSpan::ResidentSurfaceStore`, the eager
`CopyNow` plan and native planar surfaces) submits the same copy
(`engine::prefetch_target_readback`: same barrier, same slot acquisition,
appended to the open batch) and keeps the staging slot as a lease that no
ring entry owns, with the completion-timeline point of its submission. The
Store body itself - `store_render_frame` on every rail, the
`stamp_guest_write_gen` and `publish_surface_store` milestones - runs later
(`runtime::async_store`), unchanged; the target readers consume the
prefetched copy for that identity instead of recording a new one.
Ordering: (1) a completion word due behind an unlanded Store is parked in
`drain::publish_word` and published, in order and folded per slot, once
every Store deferred before it has landed, so the guest never sees a
completion before the pixels and never frees or recycles the surface
(the hazard of the earlier deferred window, which landed after stamps);
(2) every writeback-debt payment site lands first: a mapping-named access
(`pay_for_mapping`, hence every `settle_for_mapping`, the skipping BGRA
writer) through the newest Store into that mapping or into any page it
shares, a texture-named or unnamed one (`pay_for_texture`, `pay_all`) all
of them; blits, compute records and presents land all of them; (3) every
packet except `EXEC_INDIRECT2`/`NOP` lands all of them first, as do a
`REPLACE_PHYSICAL` at its arrival and a mapper ring request; a Store that is
not deferred lands all of them before it runs, and a draw into a surface
with a deferred Store lands it first. Landing is in Store order and
re-resolves the destination from the mapping table then.
Liveness: each drain pass starts and ends by landing what is ready; the end
asks the stamp completion thread (new wake entries, `install_drain_wake`)
to schedule the drain at the oldest copy's timeline point, else lands all;
the device poll reschedules a drain that still owes anything; a Store older
than 250 ms is landed waiting. Teardown returns prefetched leases before
it waits for leases. `REIMS_VGPU_ASYNC_READBACK=off` restores the
synchronous Store.
Census (`store_routes`): async_store_deferred, async_store_declined_*,
async_store_land_<site>{,_us} for ready/packet/redraw/mapping/texture/
unnamed/command/capacity/declined/no_wake/stale, async_store_age_us,
async_store_word_parked/released/folded, async_store_word_park_us,
async_store_wake_armed/unavailable, async_store_poll_reschedule,
async_store_lost, async_readback_consume_wait_us,
async_readback_copied_at_prefetch, async_readback_abandoned_teardown.
Tests: unit `runtime::async_store::tests` (9: word waits for exactly the
Stores before it, no overtaking, per-slot folding, domains never fold,
mapping depth, page overlap, aliasing reach, dense order, in-progress Store
still holds its words),
`runtime::drain::tests::async_store_words` (3, real publish path: parked
word reaches the stamp page only when the Store lands; a drain pass lands
and releases; idle publishes at once), `engine::async_readback::tests` (2),
`stamp_completion::drain_wake_tests` (2), `draw::vulkan`
`async_store_eligibility_tests` (1); GPU `vk_engine_parity::
a_prefetched_store_readback_is_the_frame_of_its_store_and_is_read_once` on
RADV NAVI21 (a draw recorded after the prefetch does not reach it, copied
and leased readers each consume it once, the next reader sees the resident
as drawn since, an unread prefetch drops).

