+//! Render Stores whose readback does not block the drain.
+//!
+//! # What changes
+//!
+//! On a host that cannot import guest RAM every render Store reads its
+//! resident back through a staging buffer and writes the guest's pages on the
+//! CPU, and the drain worker used to wait the GPU for that readback in the
+//! middle of the Store: heavy minutes spent ~460 ms of every drain
+//! second there, holding the device lock and the QEMU main loop, while the GPU
+//! was busy 17 ms a second.
+//!
+//! With this rail a surface Store submits its copy (`engine::prefetch_target_readback`)
+//! and returns. The rest of the Store — the guest-page write through the same
+//! `store_render_frame` rail as before, the publish milestones — runs later,
+//! here, when the copy's completion-timeline point has been reached: on a later
+//! drain pass woken by the completion thread, or earlier when an ordering point
+//! below forces it. The bytes written and the pages they land in are the same;
+//! only the moment moves.
+//!
+//! # The ordering argument
+//!
+//! A Store's guest writeback was observable at three kinds of place, and each
+//! one now lands every deferred Store that precedes it:
+//!
+//! 1. **The guest learning the work completed.** The guest may read a surface
+//!    with its CPU after, and only after, the completion stamp of the command
+//!    buffer that rendered it (`writeback_debt`'s doc: iOS reads icon surfaces
+//!    after completion without naming them). So a completion word that becomes
+//!    due while any Store deferred before it is unlanded is *parked*
+//!    ([`park_word`]) and published, in order, when those Stores have landed.
+//!    This is the same promise the GPU-ordered stamp rail makes, kept by the
+//!    drain instead of a queue point: the word is never in the page before the
+//!    pixels are. Because the guest cannot know the Store finished, it also
+//!    cannot have freed or recycled the surface's pages — the hazard that sank
+//!    the earlier deferred window, which landed *after* stamps
+//!    (`render_writeback`'s "it corrupts the guest's page tables").
+//! 2. **Device-side readers and writers of guest pages.** Every one already
+//!    pays the lazy writeback ledger first (`writeback_debt::pay_for_mapping`,
+//!    `pay_for_texture`, `pay_all`, and through them every `settle_*`), so
+//!    those sites land here first: a mapping-named access lands through the
+//!    newest Store into that mapping *or into any page it shares* (two mapping
+//!    ids can name one allocation), a texture-named or unnamed access lands
+//!    all of them. Blits and compute records land all of them before they run,
+//!    and so does a present, after its rescue drains and before it freezes the
+//!    presented pages.
+//! 3. **Anything that can change what a Store would do.** Every packet other
+//!    than a command-buffer submission (`EXEC_INDIRECT2`) and a NOP lands all of
+//!    them first, so no map, unmap, delete, synchronize or display packet runs
+//!    between a Store and its write; a re-point (`REPLACE_PHYSICAL`) lands them
+//!    at its arrival, where it moves the pages, and so does a mapper ring
+//!    request. A Store that is not deferred lands all of them before it runs.
+//!    A draw into a surface with a deferred Store lands it first, so the
+//!    resident still holds exactly the Store's frame when the Store's
+//!    bookkeeping (`finish`'s epoch stamp, sole-copy release) runs, and a
+//!    second Store into one surface is never reordered behind the first.
+//!
+//! Landing is always in Store order, so two Stores whose pages alias land in
+//! the order the guest issued them. The copy itself was recorded at the Store,
+//! behind the draws that produced the frame and ahead of anything later, so
+//! the staging buffer holds the Store's frame whatever the drain did since;
+//! later GPU commands that read the resident are queue-ordered after the copy
+//! exactly as before.
+//!
+//! Each landing re-resolves its destination from the mapping table *then*
+//! (the "defer the decision, not the plan" shape `render_writeback` names as
+//! the one its four panics do not rule out). Nothing above ever lets a packet
+//! that could change that table run in between.
+//!
+//! # Liveness
+//!
+//! A deferred Store must not wait for unrelated guest activity: a guest asleep
+//! on a parked word sends nothing. So the end of every tranche lands what is
+//! ready and asks the completion thread to wake the drain at the oldest copy's
+//! timeline point ([`after_tranche`]); without a completion thread it lands
+//! everything at once, which is the synchronous rail. The device poll
+//! reschedules a drain that still owes anything ([`owes_drain`]) as a backstop.
+//!
+//! `REIMS_VGPU_ASYNC_READBACK=off` restores the synchronous Store.
+
+use std::collections::VecDeque;
+
+use crate::model::DeviceState;
+use crate::runtime::host::{HostMemory, HostOps};
+use crate::runtime::resident_target::ResidentTarget;
+
+/// Deferred Stores at once. Matches the engine's in-flight cap, which is what
+/// bounds the staging memory held out of the pool.
+pub const MAX_PENDING: usize = 4;
+
+/// How long a deferred Store may wait for its copy before a drain pass lands
+/// it regardless, waiting if it must. A copy takes a few milliseconds; this
+/// only bounds the cases that are not a copy in flight — a submission whose
+/// point the queue will never signal, a wake that was lost — so that no
+/// completion word can be parked indefinitely.
+pub const STALE_AFTER: std::time::Duration = std::time::Duration::from_millis(250);
+
+/// Whether this process defers Stores at all. Read once, for the reason
+/// `lazy_writeback_enabled` is: a boot that flipped it midway would be two
+/// devices in one log.
+pub fn enabled() -> bool {
+    use std::sync::OnceLock;
+    static ON: OnceLock<bool> = OnceLock::new();
+    *ON.get_or_init(|| {
+        let (state, value) = crate::config::read(crate::config::ASYNC_READBACK);
+        let on = !matches!(state, crate::config::Switch::Off);
+        crate::observe::off(format!(
+            "async_readback on={on} switch={state:?} value={}",
+            value.unwrap_or_else(|| "<unset>".into())
+        ));
+        on
+    })
+}
+
+/// One surface Store whose copy is submitted and whose guest write is owed.
+#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
+pub struct PendingStore {
+    /// Store order. Dense: the n-th deferred Store is `n`.
+    pub seq: u64,
+    /// The resident the draw rendered into, verbatim — never re-derived, for
+    /// the reason `WritebackDebt::target` records.
+    pub target: ResidentTarget,
+    pub mapping_id: u32,
+    pub width: u32,
+    pub height: u32,
+    /// The colour attachment's declared format, for the publish milestones.
+    pub format: u16,
+    /// The guest pages the Store will write, ascending and deduplicated, as
+    /// the mapping named them when it was deferred; `None` when they could not
+    /// all be named, which overlaps everything. The mapping cannot change
+    /// before the Store lands (every packet that could change it lands it
+    /// first), so this is also where it will land.
+    pub pages: Option<std::sync::Arc<[u64]>>,
+    pub deferred_at: std::time::Instant,
+}
+
+/// Whether two ascending page lists share a page. Either side unknown shares
+/// everything: an unnamed reader cannot be ruled out, and neither can a Store
+/// whose destination could not be named.
+fn pages_overlap(a: Option<&[u64]>, b: Option<&[u64]>) -> bool {
+    let (Some(a), Some(b)) = (a, b) else {
+        return true;
+    };
+    let (Some(&a_lo), Some(&a_hi), Some(&b_lo), Some(&b_hi)) =
+        (a.first(), a.last(), b.first(), b.last())
+    else {
+        // An empty list names no page, so it reaches none.
+        return false;
+    };
+    if a_hi < b_lo || b_hi < a_lo {
+        return false;
+    }
+    let (mut i, mut j) = (0, 0);
+    while i < a.len() && j < b.len() {
+        match a[i].cmp(&b[j]) {
+            std::cmp::Ordering::Less => i += 1,
+            std::cmp::Ordering::Greater => j += 1,
+            std::cmp::Ordering::Equal => return true,
+        }
+    }
+    false
+}
+
+/// A mapping's pages as [`PendingStore::pages`] holds them.
+fn sorted_pages(state: &DeviceState, mapping_id: u32) -> Option<std::sync::Arc<[u64]>> {
+    let mut pages = state.mapping_reach_pages(mapping_id)?;
+    pages.sort_unstable();
+    pages.dedup();
+    Some(pages.into())
+}
+
+/// A completion word that became due behind deferred Stores.
+#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
+pub struct ParkedWord {
+    /// Every Store with a smaller `seq` must land before this word.
+    pub after: u64,
+    /// The publishing domain, as `drain::publish_word` takes it: the root FIFO
+    /// or a child channel.
+    pub domain: u32,
+    pub slot: u32,
+    pub value: u32,
+}
+
+/// Why a landing happened, for the census. Every forced site is named, so a
+/// boot says which ordering point is costing the overlap.
+#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
+pub enum LandSite {
+    /// The copy was complete when the drain looked: no wait.
+    Ready,
+    /// A packet other than a submission.
+    Packet,
+    /// A draw into the surface the Store targets.
+    Redraw,
+    /// A host reader or writer naming the mapping.
+    Mapping,
+    /// A texture-named reader; it may alias any surface's pages.
+    Texture,
+    /// A reader that names nothing.
+    Unnamed,
+    /// A blit or compute record.
+    Command,
+    /// The in-flight cap.
+    Capacity,
+    /// A later Store could not be deferred and must not overtake.
+    Declined,
+    /// No wake could be armed at the end of a tranche.
+    NoWake,
+    /// Deferred longer than [`STALE_AFTER`].
+    Stale,
+}
+
+impl LandSite {
+    fn route(self) -> &'static str {
+        match self {
+            Self::Ready => "async_store_land_ready",
+            Self::Packet => "async_store_land_packet",
+            Self::Redraw => "async_store_land_redraw",
+            Self::Mapping => "async_store_land_mapping",
+            Self::Texture => "async_store_land_texture",
+            Self::Unnamed => "async_store_land_unnamed",
+            Self::Command => "async_store_land_command",
+            Self::Capacity => "async_store_land_capacity",
+            Self::Declined => "async_store_land_declined",
+            Self::NoWake => "async_store_land_no_wake",
+            Self::Stale => "async_store_land_stale",
+        }
+    }
+
+    fn route_us(self) -> &'static str {
+        match self {
+            Self::Ready => "async_store_land_ready_us",
+            Self::Packet => "async_store_land_packet_us",
+            Self::Redraw => "async_store_land_redraw_us",
+            Self::Mapping => "async_store_land_mapping_us",
+            Self::Texture => "async_store_land_texture_us",
+            Self::Unnamed => "async_store_land_unnamed_us",
+            Self::Command => "async_store_land_command_us",
+            Self::Capacity => "async_store_land_capacity_us",
+            Self::Declined => "async_store_land_declined_us",
+            Self::NoWake => "async_store_land_no_wake_us",
+            Self::Stale => "async_store_land_stale_us",
+        }
+    }
+}
